      "contentPreview": "GENUINE EFFICIENCY FINDING, strengthened by the correction above: LoadIndex opens a file handle on every call, even on a pure in-memory-cache hit, and 19 of its 20 callers are read-only. FileMemoryStore.LoadIndex (src/Scrinia.Core/FileMemoryStore.cs:576) calls FileLock.AcquireShared(GetLockPath(scope)) \u2014 an OS file-handle open \u2014 unconditionally, BEFORE LoadIndexUnsafe (:589) ever checks the in-memory cache at :592-593. So every LoadIndex call pays a filesystem lock-acquire even when the cache wo",
